---
/* DRAFT-FOR-ED — candidate node page, /next preview namespace. */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import MarkNote from '../../components/MarkNote.astro'

export const prerender = true
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Hand-drawn layouts"
  description="Web pages drawn by hand in a notebook first, then built responsive."
>
  <article class="node">
    <p class="draft-stamp">draft · under review</p>
    <header data-mark="hdl:masthead">
      <h1>Hand-drawn layouts</h1>
      <p class="dek">Draw the page in a notebook. Then make the browser honor the drawing.</p>
      <p class="meta">craft · experiment · hand drawing, HTML, Remotion</p>
    </header>

    <section data-mark="hdl:what">
      <h2>The experiment</h2>
      <p>
        A page layout gets drawn by hand first — boxes, arrows, a walking figure, the
        handwriting slanting where it wants to. Then the drawing is rebuilt as a
        responsive web page: same composition, same proportions, honest to the original
        down to its irregularities, but reflowing properly on a phone. A comparison view
        pairs each drawn source with its built result.
      </p>
      <p>
        One drawing kept going: a hand-drawn walk cycle became a rendered animation, the
        notebook figure moving in a programmatic video. The through-line is the same as
        the handwriting pipeline's — the hand decides first, and the machine's job is
        fidelity to that decision, not improvement of it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section data-mark="hdl:status">
      <h2>Where it stands</h2>
      <p>
        An experiment with finished pieces: drawn sources, built pages, one animation.
        The comparison gallery will appear here once its images are prepared for the
        public page.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
  <MarkNote />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .node {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-12) var(--page-gutter) var(--space-24);
  }
  .draft-stamp {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-8);
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--font-size-2xl);
    line-height: var(--leading-tight);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
  }
  .dek {
    font-size: var(--font-size-md);
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
  }
  .meta {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-8);
  }
  h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    margin: var(--space-8) 0 var(--space-4);
  }
  p {
    line-height: var(--leading-normal);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }
</style>
